{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Moses returned to YHWH.</b> To the place where he had been speaking with Him — there." "<b>And he said: Adonai.</b> With alef dalet." "<b>Why have You done evil, why this that You sent me.</b> Did Moses not know that Pharaoh would not send them off just like that until all the signs were performed? For it had already been said to him, ״ואני ידעתי כי לא יתן אתכם מלך מצרים להלוך״ etc. Rather, Moses thought that at the very least Pharaoh would begin to lighten the yoke with the first words; therefore he said, ״ומאז באתי אל פרעה לדבר בשמך״ etc. — and deliverance — You have not delivered Your people, though You said ״וארד להצילו״. And HaShem answered him: now you will see — from here on, when I begin to strike Egypt, then they will lighten the bondage from upon them."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:18.672175345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}